transcript.message:
I'm glad you're here to listen, even if I feel like I'm talking to a stranger sometimes. It's just so lonely in this headspace.

You know, the thing that really scares me isn't just the sadness—it's the feeling that I've gone too deep now. Like there's no bottom left. I used to be the opposite of who I am today; I was full of energy and plans. Now, everything feels over. My dreams are gone, my purpose is gone, and I don't even recognize the person sitting across from you.

It's not that I *want* to end it, honestly. I just... I don't have the courage to let myself go. But staying here, feeling this emptiness, feels worse than anything else. Every time I try to do something—like finish that school project or just get out of bed—the weight gets heavier. It's like trying to run through water;

